  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "Formal written English uses set phrases: 'I am writing to inform you that ...', 'Please find attached ...', 'Should you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact me.' These phrases signal professionalism in emails and reports.",
    "explanation_ko": "격식체 문어체 영어는 정형화된 표현을 씁니다: 'I am writing to inform you that ...', 'Please find attached ...', 'Should you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact me.' 이런 표현은 이메일·보고서에서 전문성을 나타냅니다.",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "I am writing to inform you that the meeting has been rescheduled.",
        "ko": "회의 일정이 변경되었음을 알려드리고자 메일 드립니다."
      },
      {
        "en": "Please find attached the report you requested.",
        "ko": "요청하신 보고서를 첨부해 드립니다."
      },
      {
        "en": "Should you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact me.",
        "ko": "궁금하신 점이 있으시면 언제든지 연락 주세요."
      }
    ]
  },
